    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0328" n="314" xml:id="pg314"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Indonesia/3–1049: Telegram.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consulate General at
                        Batavia </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-10T21:00:00-05:00">March 10, 1949—9
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155. Usgoc 329. Dept requests your comments Niact on Stikker–Bevin letter which
                    assume you have already received from Brit Con-Gen. Question which Dept must now
                    answer is whether US should tell Stikker that we consider these proposals
                    reasonable as basis removal Jogja obstacle and as preliminary to round table
                    discussions, subject to bona fide negotiations in Batavia of details requiring
                    negotiation. Neths Ambassador has made clear that unless US and Brit can so
                    inform Stikker, Stikker would not attempt gain Dutch Govt approval this
                    program.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
